  "assumption_notes": [
    "Historical source balances are August 31, 2025. The October 31 model opening is an explicit unchanged-balance proxy, not actual closing accounts. Intervening operating cash flows, dividends and dispositions require a reviewed closing bridge.",
    "Forecasts are full 12-month model years ending October 31, not issuer fiscal years. The information cutoff is October 31, 2025; source retrieval occurred November 22, 2026.",
    "Forecast growth and margins are analyst scenarios, not management guidance. Forecast gross margin is before D&A; historical reported gross margin contains some D&A.",
    "Other current assets, goodwill, ROU assets, deferred taxes and remaining other assets/liabilities are held constant. Held-for-sale balances and cloud assets are frozen; disposal proceeds and cloud capitalization require separate forecasts for actual use.",
    "Forecast PPE depreciation uses the rounded $7.6 million FY2025 note disclosure divided by reported opening net PPE. Finite-intangible amortization is $0.183 million annually. Cash-flow D&A includes other items and is not exact PPE depreciation.",
    "Cash capex is assumed at 1.5% of sales versus reported FY2025 PPE purchases of about 0.73%. Historical accrued and noncash additions remain in the source data.",
    "The FY2025 $11.929 million tax benefit is not repeated. A 23% tax rate, 80% NOL utilization limit and fully deductible interest are modeling conventions, not jurisdiction-specific tax calculations.",
    "Standalone SBC is expensed, added back to CFO and settled in new shares at the flat $194.28 price assumption. DCF and acquisition retain its cost as cash-equivalent compensation; do not also apply the same future award dilution to those equity values.",
    "WACC components of 4% risk-free rate, 0.9 beta, 5.5% equity risk premium, 6% pretax debt cost and 10% target debt weight are illustrative analyst inputs, not verified October 31 market estimates.",
    "Full reported cash is used in the equity bridge. Cash availability and operating-cash classification require review.",
    "The $1.1 million other-claim amount is a rounded uncertain-tax-liability proxy. DCF and comparables deduct it; acquisition assumes settlement at closing. Actual settlement amount and timing remain unverified.",
    "Acquisition entry EV uses the $194.28 reference price with a hypothetical 20% control premium, common shares and identified claims. It is not a seller acceptance, financing quote or transaction announcement.",
    "Initial term debt is 3 times operating EBIT plus cash-flow D&A: 3 times $111.984 million. This differs from issuer adjusted EBITDA of $114.426 million. Debt terms and the 18 times exit EBITDA multiple are hypothetical.",
    "Independent qualified human validation remains outstanding. The source dataset, closing balances, assumptions, employer acceptance and operational release gates require review before live use."
